Use `useChatRuntime` from `@assistant-ui/ai-sdk` and pass the runtime to `AssistantRuntimeProvider`. This requires `ai@^7` and `@ai-sdk/react@^4`; v4–v6 have separate legacy pages, which I didn't read.

Your route should accept `messages` (`UIMessage[]`), pass `await convertToModelMessages(messages)` to `streamText`, and return:

```ts
return createUIMessageStreamResponse({
  stream: toUIMessageStream({ stream: result.stream }),
});
```

The web example uses `app/api/chat/route.ts` with plain `useChatRuntime()`. For another path, set `transport: new AssistantChatTransport({ api: "/your/path" })`.

`AssistantChatTransport`, the default, also sends `system` and `tools`. To use them, pass `system` to `streamText`, and include `frontendTools(tools)` in its tools and in `convertToModelMessages`' `{ tools }` option. For chained tool calls, set `stopWhen`, such as `stepCountIs(10)`.

Pages: docs/runtimes/ai-sdk/v7.md
